※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4507

※ The four roundings answer the whole number a floating-point number rounds to.
※ An integer is a whole number already, so rounding one would answer with what
※ it was handed -- which is a question nobody asks and an operator nobody
※ writes on purpose.

@[startup]
fn main() → u8:
    let n: u8 = 5u8
    let rounded: u8 = ↓n
    0u8
